  bootwright / preflight infra
      Check the readiness of the infrastructure the Environment declares: the controller checks
      of preflight controller for the selected context, including the firewall admission of the
      controller's managed service sockets, and the capacity of the hosts that hold the
      context's Machines. It reports only what it observes: external services, a Registry or
      LoadBalancer and managed services on other Machines are not checked, and apply checks
      them itself. It takes no cluster selection and no SSH or trust options, because it
      observes the controller and the local hosts only.

  Usage
    bootwright preflight infra [flags]

  Command flags
      --dry-run  Limit work to the command's dry-run boundary

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright preflight infra --context lab --output json
